Dear members of the NBLAST team,

I have a set of neurons represented in SWC format. I would like to compare them using NBLAST. I have the following questions:

1. I understand that NBLAST required input neurons to be represented as a set of point-tangent vector pairs. Could you point me to some documentation on this representation? The NBLAST-paper refers to Masse et.al <http://et.al>. 2012 for this, but I could not figure out the input format from this paper.

2. Is there a way to convert SWC files to point-tangent vector format so as to apply NBLAST on them?

Thanks
Ajay

